The QA test defines the two dataclass instances directly with literal keyword arguments. `SELF_TARGET` is created with `client="chrome"`, `version="110"`, `os="windows"`, and `os_version="10"`, while `OTHER_TARGET` is created with `client="chrome"`, `version="100"`, `os=None`, and `os_version=None`. In `ImpersonateTarget.__contains__`, the expression `OTHER_TARGET in SELF_TARGET` means `self` is `SELF_TARGET` and `target` is `OTHER_TARGET`, and the return condition reads exactly those eight attributes.

## Answer
{"self_client":"chrome","self_os":"windows","self_os_version":"10","self_version":"110","target_client":"chrome","target_os":null,"target_os_version":null,"target_version":"100"}
